  "notes": [
    "added by the ADR 0009 amendment (2026-08-16), which bounds the volatile TTL",
    "31 years vs 3600 seconds behaved identically before the amendment, which is the hole: \u00a77's 'the declared TTL is present evidence' argument holds only while the declaration is bounded.",
    "No invalidation block: the edge is already unknown before any mutation, so there is nothing for a mutation to demonstrate.",
    "The sibling case -- an observed_at dated in the future -- is covered by crates/freshdag-engine/src/tests.rs::a_future_observed_at_is_not_evidence and NOT by a scenario, because the harness derives its injected clock from the newest event timestamp and so cannot express a checking clock behind the observation. Expressing it as a fixture needs a scenario-level `now`, which is a schemas/scenario change."
  ]
